.TH START-RAAT 1 "October 2025" "HiFiBerry OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
start-raat \- start RAAT (Roon Advanced Audio Transport) service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start-raat
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B start-raat
is a wrapper script that starts the RAAT (Roon Advanced Audio Transport) service
with proper configuration and environment setup for HiFiBerry devices.
.PP
The script performs the following operations:
.IP \(bu 2
Checks if Avahi daemon is running and waits up to 30 seconds for it to become available
.IP \(bu 2
Determines the appropriate configuration directory (per-user or system-wide)
.IP \(bu 2
Checks write permissions for /var/lib/raat for metadata pipe functionality
.IP \(bu 2
Creates necessary configuration directories
.IP \(bu 2
Runs configure-raat to generate the RAAT configuration
.IP \(bu 2
Starts the RAAT application with trace logging enabled
.SH CONFIGURATION
The script uses different configuration directories depending on the runtime environment:
.TP
.B User service mode
Configuration stored in ~/.raat
.TP
.B System service mode
Configuration stored in /var/lib/raat
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.raat/
Per-user RAAT configuration directory
.TP
.I /var/lib/raat/
System-wide RAAT configuration directory
.TP
.I /var/lib/raat/hifiberry.conf
Generated RAAT configuration file
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
If set, indicates user service mode
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_ID
If set, indicates user service mode
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.B avahi-daemon
Required for mDNS functionality
.TP
.B configure-raat
Configuration generator script
.TP
.B raat_app
The main RAAT application binary
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR configure-raat (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR avahi-daemon (8)
.SH AUTHOR
HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>